          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "UK's NCSC warns AI-powered bug hunting will unleash a patch tsunami of long-buried code vulnerabilities",
            "articleSection": "Policy & Rights",
            "abstract": "Britain's National Cyber Security Centre has issued a warning that AI-assisted vulnerability discovery is rapidly surfacing decades of previously undetected software flaws, creating a wave of urgent patches that security teams will struggle to absorb. The agency says years of accumulated technical debt in codebases — shortcuts and legacy decisions made by developers under time pressure — are now being exposed at machine speed. Organisations are advised to prioritise patch management infrastructure and incident response capacity before the volume of disclosures overwhelms them.",
            "url": "https://go.theregister.com/feed/www.theregister.com/2026/05/02/ncsc_brace_for_patch_tsunami/",
            "publisher": {
              "@type": "NewsMediaOrganization",
              "name": "The AI Chronicle",
